{"text":"E1 source closure has one bounded opaque-capability question. No broader port refusal or new origin kind has been implemented.\n\nThe shared provenance hook now covers both operand paths, structural item selection, effect leaf copies, expected revisions, wire/list/key/hash consumers and lazy opaque fields/args/from/fromItems. The shipped ordinary capabilities read item/page/record(s)/recordCount plus scope/intent; those supported paths have explicit provenance. Existing ActRecords protects marked record values.\n\nA caller-supplied capability can also call the full StateView interface: all(), holders(), pendingRequests(), lookup() and other bookkeeping ports. Those can expose private positions or require hypothetical request/account data that the item-only after view cannot truthfully supply. Returning the recorded-only list could be incomplete; exposing private addresses is also wrong. The current Origin union describes row/slot/revision/opened positions, not a new symbolic request/account model.\n\nProposed boundary: retain known complete recorded data and supported item/record reads. When a capability actually calls a port or reads a metadata field whose answer needs unrepresented hypothetical entry/bookkeeping data, return unavailable/lacks entry. Keep it lazy at the reached read; do not reject a capability merely because it receives a view, and reuse row protection where all().items can truthfully expose the same item view. Do not add symbolic requests/accounts, a second evaluator, or a blanket capability ban.\n\nConfirm that bounded unavailability rule, or name additional E1 port data that must be projected now. The no-hook runtime path and4,029recorded answers remain unchanged. Independent shipped-consumer wiring continues.\n\nThis replaces unclaimed request e05150d21836049e02771732a3cf9a72134cfe31 because inherited retired bases mark it stale in the default queue. The cited decisions and source findings remain current references, carried here as text rather than stale content bases. No policy disposition is implied. Since the original question, Core E1's implemented slice passed its bounded development sequence at a16efe66, while the client wrapper remains incomplete. C3 has only an external, unexecuted witness design in preparation. The builder still holds the policy or production change pending the planner's answer.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on reached opaque StateView metadata/bookkeeping reads that require unrepresented hypothetical data: proposed lazy unavailable/lacks entry, preserving known recorded and supported item/record reads without a new symbolic request/account model.","no_git_artifact":"true","replaces":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e05150d21836049e02771732a3cf9a72134cfe31","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"},"expectation":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e05150d21836049e02771732a3cf9a72134cfe31","retirement":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:577b9b7959b7aa91430699b7fa173b3a1d861188","promise":"absent","completion":"absent"}}